maya: Quick heads-up — I'm planning a small StatefulSet tweak for inference-workers to smooth rolling drains. Intend to bump minReadySeconds to 30, add a soft preStop drain, and change the PDB to allow 1 unavailable. TF change is staged. Any red flags?

alex: Sounds reasonable. Are we changing desired replicas or just the PDB/minReady? We can't go below 3 replicas in prod.

maya: Just PDB/minReady + a tiny readiness probe tweak (increase successThreshold). No replica change for prod. Will target canary namespace first.

satoshi: Question: how are you planning to do the canary? Suggest partitioned StatefulSet rollout so we can flip the last two pods first. That way we avoid full cluster churn. Example: set .spec.updateStrategy.rollingUpdate.partition = 1 (or 2 depending on count).

liam: Also confirm preStop hook will drain in-flight requests gracefully. For inference we should wait for the current batch/prefix to finish — preStop should call /drain endpoint and sleep. Any chance of traffic spike during rollout window?

maya: Good call. preStop will hit local /_admin/drain then sleep 15s. Probe changes = successThreshold: 3 -> 5 to avoid flapping during short drain. Canary window planned 2h starting 03:00 UTC tomorrow (low traffic).

maya: Terraform diff (staged):
```hcl
resource "kubernetes_stateful_set" "inference_workers" {
  metadata { name = "inference-workers" }
  spec {
    update_strategy {
      type = "RollingUpdate"
      rolling_update { partition = 1 }
    }
    min_ready_seconds = 30
    template {
      spec {
        termination_grace_period_seconds = 40
        lifecycle { pre_stop { exec { command = ["/bin/sh","-c","curl -sS http://localhost:8080/_admin/drain || true; sleep 15"] } } }
      }
    }
  }
}
resource "kubernetes_pod_disruption_budget" "inference_pdb" {
  spec {
    min_available = null
    max_unavailable = 1
    selector { match_labels = { app = "inference" } }
  }
}
```

alex: That looks fine. One small nit: if we set max_unavailable = 1 and have only 3 replicas, we could end up with 2 available during rolling if partitioning misaligns. Recommend partition=1 and double-check pod ordinal order before apply.

satoshi: Also remember to pin the rollout to the canary node pool by nodeSelector/affinity so we don't evict critical prod nodes. Use label: inference-canary=true.

liam: Secrets/KMS check — are you touching env vars or volume mounts? If the image reads KMS keys on startup we may need a quick restart, which could interfere.

maya: Not touching secrets. Just lifecycle/probes/pdb. Confirmed.

infra-bot: terraform plan for workspace "staging" completed: 2 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy. No drift detected. :white_check_mark:

alex: I'll do a quick review in ~30m. Ping me when you push the PR and include the kubectl steps for manual rollback.

maya: Will do. Manual rollback steps I'll include:
```bash
# rollback partition -> 0 to force full roll back to previous revision (or kubectl rollout undo)
kubectl -n staging patch statefulset inference-workers -p '{"spec":{"updateStrategy":{"rollingUpdate":{"partition":0}}}}'
# or
kubectl -n staging rollout undo sts/inference-workers
```

maya: Plan: open PR now, await review, apply to staging canary at 03:00 UTC tomorrow for 2h window. If no regressions, promote to prod next night with partition=2 for gradual flip.

satoshi: LGTM — small checklist: (1) nodeSelector for canary, (2) ensure HPA target won't fight partitioned pods, (3) add alert for >1 pod in CrashLoopBackOff during window.

maya: Adding those to PR description. @alex please review when free. Thanks all. :pray:
